  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.45.0\"\n\nrecipe:\n  name: goose\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 7ab566796ba276b987d655fdee0fbbf50e821a2c1314fcca66ef91b128983e8b\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\noutputs:\n  - package:\n      name: goose-cli\n      version: ${{ version }}\n    build:\n      script:\n        - if: win\n          then: |\n            set CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja\n            set CMAKE_GENERATOR_TOOLSET=\n            set CMAKE_GENERATOR_PLATFORM=\n            set \"CMAKE_ARGS=%CMAKE_ARGS:-DCMAKE_GENERATOR_TOOLSET=v143=%\"\n            set \"CMAKE_ARGS=%CMAKE_ARGS:-DCMAKE_GENERATOR_PLATFORM=x64=%\"\n            pushd crates\\goose-cli\n            cargo-bundle-licenses --format yaml --output ${{ SRC_DIR }}\\THIRDPARTY.yml\n          else: |\n            export CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja\n            export RUSTFLAGS=\"-Clink-arg=-L${PREFIX}/lib -Clink-arg=-lomp\"\n            pushd crates/goose-cli\n            cargo-bundle-licenses --format yaml --output ${{ SRC_DIR }}/THIRDPARTY.yml\n        - cargo install --no-track --locked --root ${{ PREFIX }} --path .\n        - popd\n    requirements:\n      build:\n        - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n        - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n        - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n        - ${{ 'clangdev' if build_platform != target_platform }}\n        - ${{ 'protobuf' if linux }}\n        - cargo-bundle-licenses\n        - cmake\n        - ninja\n        - pkg-config\n      host:\n        - ${{ 'llvm-openmp' if osx }}\n        - if: linux\n          then:\n            - dbus\n            - libxcb\n        - clangdev\n        - zlib\n    tests:\n      - script:\n          - goose --version\n          - goose --help\n          - goose serve --help\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://goose-docs.ai\n  documentation: https://goose-docs.ai/docs\n  repository: https://github.com/aaif-goose/goose\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  summary: 'An open source, extensible AI agent that goes beyond code suggestions - install, execute, edit, and test with any LLM'\n  description: |\n    goose is a general-purpose AI agent that runs on your machine.\n    Not just for code — use it for research, writing, automation, data analysis, or anything you need to get done.\n\n    goose works with 15+ providers — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Ollama, OpenRouter, Azure, Bedrock, and more.\n    Use API keys or your existing Claude, ChatGPT, or Gemini subscriptions via [ACP](https://goose-docs.ai/docs/guides/acp-providers).\n    Connect to 70+ extensions via the [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) open standard.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - eunos-1128\n",
